Third-party notices

1. Vocabulary data in data/vocab.json is derived from qwerty-learner
   (https://github.com/Kaiyiwing/qwerty-learner), which is licensed under the
   MIT License. Copyright (c) qwerty-learner contributors.
   The derived file shortens definitions to at most three senses and derives
   two subsets (CET-4 minus GaoKao-3500, CET-6 minus CET-4).

2. Reading items in data/reading.json link to articles published by
   ScienceDaily, Aeon and Our World in Data. Only titles, canonical URLs,
   source names and estimated reading time are stored; no article text is
   reproduced. All rights remain with the original publishers.

3. Listening items in data/listening.json reference public videos on Bilibili.
   Only titles, URLs, uploader-visible duration and a category label are
   stored; no video or audio content is reproduced.

4. Translation and writing prompts in data/translation_*.json and
   data/writing_*.json are rewritten from past exam themes; the model essays
   and reference translations are original work of this project.
